spec:
  summary: |
    Input has n colored objects on a black grid, with a legend (one singleton pixel per color)
    in the rightmost column at rows 0..n-1. Output is an n x n pairwise relation table:
    2x2 color labels on top/left edges, RED (2) for same dihedral shape, GREY (5) otherwise,
    diagonal blank, all separated by 1-cell bg gaps. Output size = (3n+2) x (3n+2).
  grid: 20-25 rows x 20-23 cols, large enough for n non-overlapping objects + legend column
  background: 0 (black)
  n: 4-7 foreground colors
  legend:
    position: rightmost column, rows 0 through n-1, one singleton pixel per color
    colors: each unique, never RED (2) or GREY (5)
    ordering: determines row/column order in output table
  objects:
    count: exactly n, one per legend color
    shape: 4-connected monochromatic, area 5-13, bbox 2-7 rows x 2-7 cols
    no_enclosed_holes: true
    placement: non-overlapping, min Manhattan gap >= 3, all within cols 0..W-2 (avoid legend col)
    each_color_appears_twice: once as main object (area > 1), once as legend singleton
  equivalence_classes:
    count: 2-3 distinct dihedral shape classes
    class_sizes: 1-3 members each; at least one class has >= 2 members
    shapes_within_class: same mask under rotation/reflection but typically different orientation [observed]
  output:
    size: (3n+2) x (3n+2)
    structure: header row/col of 2x2 color labels + n x n body of 2x2 RED/GREY cells, 1-cell bg separators
    diagonal: background (empty)
    off_diagonal: RED if pair shares dihedral shape, GREY otherwise

generation_strategy:
  approach: output-first
  steps:
    1. Pick n in [4,7]. Choose n distinct colors from {1,3,4,6,7,8,9} (avoid 2,5).
    2. Design 2-3 shape equivalence classes, assigning each color to a class.
       Each class gets a canonical 4-connected mask (area 5-13, bbox 2-7 x 2-7, no enclosed holes).
       For each member, apply a random rotation/flip to the canonical mask.
    3. Build output table (3n+2 x 3n+2): place 2x2 color headers, fill off-diagonal
       cells with RED or GREY per class membership, leave diagonal as bg.
    4. Build input grid (20-25 x 20-23): place the n oriented masks at random
       non-overlapping positions (all within cols 0..W-2, min gap >= 3).
       Place legend singletons in the last column at rows 0..n-1 in chosen order.
